   "html_text": "Padian & Horner (2002) offer a coarse-grained example of how a metaphysical commitment overlaps with issues of phylogenetic inference in their defense of treating Aves as the sole living branch of dinosaurs. In this case, they identify “transformationist” thinking against typological thinking. In the former, the identity of taxa is associated with historical continuity, and untethered from the expression of any intrinsic characters. Thus, the transformation of ancient theropod dinosaurs into the",
